02:50:52.540 --> 02:50:54.520
don't miss the Tonight Show with Jay Leno,

02:50:54.640 --> 02:50:56.120
then Late Night with David Letterman,

02:50:56.400 --> 02:50:57.860
followed by Friday Night Videos.

02:50:57.860 --> 02:50:59.000
Those of you on the West Coast

02:50:59.000 --> 02:50:59.960
will see two special...

02:51:00.190 --> 02:51:01.650
of The Fresh Prince.

02:51:34.790 --> 02:51:35.550
Insulence.

02:51:36.070 --> 02:51:37.530
NBC Sports.

02:51:38.390 --> 02:51:38.830
America.

02:51:49.270 --> 02:51:49.790
Sensing hammer.

02:51:50.100 --> 02:51:51.200
You should run for president.

02:51:54.810 --> 02:51:55.090
Jay.

02:51:56.080 --> 02:51:57.440
Jay really moves me.

02:51:59.200 --> 02:51:59.980
With Wendy's night.

02:52:00.120 --> 02:52:04.100
99-cent super value menu, a small stack of change gets you a big stack of beef.

02:52:04.360 --> 02:52:07.060
It's Wendy's 99-cent quarter-pound double stack.

02:52:07.660 --> 02:52:10.800
It's a quarter-pound of Wendy's fresh beef served hot off the grill,

02:52:11.360 --> 02:52:14.160
stacked with cheese, mustard, onions, pickles, and ketchup,

02:52:14.300 --> 02:52:16.700
and it's all just 99 cents every day.

02:52:16.860 --> 02:52:20.040
Johnny, I thought Phoenix started off playing very well

02:52:20.040 --> 02:52:23.000
and just continued to play very good basketball.

02:52:23.260 --> 02:52:25.900
They came out of the box. The Bulls were very, very tentative.

02:52:26.100 --> 02:52:29.840
The Bulls, you know, trailed by, what was it, 16 points, I guess.

02:52:30.000 --> 02:52:31.940
early in the game just to reverse

02:52:31.940 --> 02:52:33.880
at game one. They took the lead. The Bulls

02:52:33.880 --> 02:52:36.300
finally came back and were able to recapture

02:52:36.300 --> 02:52:38.140
the lead, but it was too late. But thanks to the

02:52:38.140 --> 02:52:40.080
heroics of John Paxson, it's good to see somebody

02:52:40.080 --> 02:52:42.440
come off the bench. John Paxson did a great

02:52:42.440 --> 02:52:44.360
job. Right now, let's go down to the interview

02:52:44.360 --> 02:52:46.280
area. Phoenix coach Paul Westphal

02:52:46.280 --> 02:52:46.920
is already there.

02:53:30.480 --> 02:53:32.280
and that that was really the difference in the game.

02:53:32.600 --> 02:53:37.540
What can you do now that you've lost road court advantage for the rest of the series?

02:53:37.980 --> 02:53:39.900
Well, that's a great question.

02:53:41.510 --> 02:53:46.780
I really believe if we're the best team, that we should be able to win two games at home and prove it.

02:53:47.460 --> 02:53:51.490
And that's what we played the whole season, to get the home court advantage.

02:53:52.340 --> 02:53:55.380
Let's just pretend like everybody held serve and we're going back home.

02:53:56.690 --> 02:53:59.970
That's the way we're looking at it, and we're figuring that that's an advantage.

02:54:00.000 --> 02:54:04.500
advantage. If we can't win two at home, we don't deserve to be the world champions and the Bulls

02:54:04.500 --> 02:54:09.820
deserve it. But we're glad that the games are on our court, despite the fact that we've lost two

02:54:09.820 --> 02:54:24.230
already. I think he was on fire tonight and things were going good. Usually I'll make changes if

02:54:24.230 --> 02:54:27.550
we're behind and I want to change the way things are going. And if we start to catch up with a

02:54:27.550 --> 02:54:29.910
different lineup, then I'll stay with that. But Richard.

02:54:30.000 --> 02:54:35.380
was sensational, and the lead was growing while he was in there, so I didn't have to

02:54:35.380 --> 02:54:42.240
make a change. I'm kind of stuck. I don't mean stuck, but I mean, I play K.J., Marley, and

02:54:42.240 --> 02:54:47.420
Charles almost all the time. Richard's not a center. That means if I make a change at

02:54:47.420 --> 02:54:52.980
center or I make a change at that spot, and he's just the odd man out sometimes, but as

02:54:52.980 --> 02:54:58.720
you can see, he's a great young player, and he really stepped up with a great performance

02:54:58.720 --> 02:54:59.060
tonight.

02:55:00.320 --> 02:55:04.540
Can you explain the fact that your team is now 5-for-5 in must-win situations?

02:55:05.280 --> 02:55:07.720
Well, I think that we have a pretty good team.

02:55:09.240 --> 02:55:12.920
And people that haven't seen us that much tend to not remember that.

02:55:13.080 --> 02:55:19.910
But we didn't win 62 games by accident, just like the Bulls didn't win two world championships by accident.

02:55:20.050 --> 02:55:26.220
These are the best two teams in basketball playing, and one of them will be the world champion.

02:55:26.380 --> 02:55:29.620
And, you know, we're definitely a good team.

02:55:30.850 --> 02:55:48.860
You just say, see us drive anybody into the floor tonight, did you?

02:55:49.760 --> 02:55:51.880
I mean, I didn't see when somebody was up in the air,

02:55:52.280 --> 02:55:56.460
us take them and give what everybody calls a hard foul and knock them down.

02:55:57.250 --> 02:55:59.830
I thought we played good defense where we stepped over.

02:56:00.000 --> 02:56:05.960
We moved our feet, tried to draw charges, tried to block shots, and played good basketball.

02:56:06.180 --> 02:56:12.580
And I think that there is a good lesson that you can win a game in the NBA without trying to drill people through the floor.

02:56:13.610 --> 02:56:19.890
And, you know, I would like some people to remember that, that this game is still a game of finesse and moving your feet.

02:56:19.930 --> 02:56:21.230
And I think that we showed that tonight.

02:56:21.690 --> 02:56:27.020
Jordan got his points, but you shut down, completely shut down Grant and Cartwright.

02:56:27.380 --> 02:56:29.840
Well, I don't know that we shut them down.

02:56:31.100 --> 02:56:34.160
So everybody from time to time, I said this one, KJ struggled.

02:56:34.900 --> 02:56:39.060
Everybody except probably Michael Jordan and maybe Charles struggles once in a while,

02:56:39.060 --> 02:56:40.240
and it was their turn to struggle.

02:56:40.320 --> 02:56:41.400
I don't know that it was what we did.

02:56:42.180 --> 02:56:48.040
Have you ever been involved in a situation where you've forced an entire city to be in a state of shock?

02:56:48.590 --> 02:56:50.410
Well, it was our goal to save the city.

02:56:50.510 --> 02:56:51.170
We like Chicago.

02:56:51.190 --> 02:56:54.230
We had had a really nice week, and we thought that we would step forward

02:56:54.230 --> 02:56:58.410
and do something for the city to pay them back for the hospitality they showed.

02:56:58.710 --> 02:56:59.910
We didn't want to see it burn today.

02:57:00.000 --> 02:57:29.960
I guess y'all can take that damn plywood off.

02:57:30.000 --> 02:57:31.380
the Wall of Wonders now.

02:57:32.060 --> 02:57:36.910
We're civilized in Phoenix.

02:57:37.030 --> 02:57:37.690
We won't riot.

02:57:38.080 --> 02:57:39.220
There's ex-Chicagoans

02:57:39.220 --> 02:57:39.980
living there, don't we?

02:57:40.540 --> 02:57:41.840
Them just rich Chicagoans

02:57:41.840 --> 02:57:42.440
who moved there.

02:57:42.800 --> 02:57:43.280
Went home.

02:57:47.550 --> 02:57:48.870
We still got to win

02:57:48.870 --> 02:57:49.630
two more games.

02:57:49.750 --> 02:57:50.590
They got to win one.

02:57:50.790 --> 02:57:52.140
It's going to be a tough series.

02:57:52.240 --> 02:57:53.040
But I tell you what,

02:57:54.200 --> 02:57:55.340
it's funny when you see

02:57:55.340 --> 02:57:56.120
the mayor and everybody

02:57:56.120 --> 02:57:56.940
get on TV talking

02:57:56.940 --> 02:57:57.980
about Don't Destroy the City.

02:57:59.020 --> 02:57:59.940
I told a guy,

02:58:00.000 --> 02:58:00.720
Let's don't play the game.

02:58:00.800 --> 02:58:02.700
Let's just get back to Phoenix in time for happy hour.

02:58:04.200 --> 02:58:06.580
You don't blame them for taking precautions, though, do you?

02:58:06.700 --> 02:58:08.460
Just in case you guys might have slipped up.

02:58:09.010 --> 02:58:14.930
Well, I think putting extra policemen out there, National Guard, whatever, would have been fine.

02:58:15.030 --> 02:58:16.150
You're boarding up winners and everything.

02:58:16.290 --> 02:58:17.170
I think that's kind of...

02:58:17.170 --> 02:58:20.020
I'm walking down Michigan Avenue, and I don't see any things in the stores.

02:58:20.950 --> 02:58:22.750
I was starting to get worried there for a second.

02:58:22.930 --> 02:58:24.230
I ain't thought I was back in the neighborhood.

02:58:26.950 --> 02:58:29.630
Hey, did that motivate you guys when you saw all those preparations?

02:58:30.000 --> 02:58:31.580
Did you say, look, have they already got us losing?

02:58:31.880 --> 02:58:33.040
I think it's no question.

02:58:33.540 --> 02:58:36.700
I thought it was fun and more than getting us motivated.

02:58:40.930 --> 02:58:43.440
Listen, this is our fifth game that our season could end.

02:58:44.200 --> 02:58:47.660
We are pretty much immune to the situation now.

02:58:48.690 --> 02:58:52.430
You have three guys with 20 or more points in this contest,

02:58:52.610 --> 02:58:55.590
and plus you did a good job of shutting down Grant on the board.

02:58:56.290 --> 02:58:59.960
Well, I think you guys will get...

02:59:00.000 --> 02:59:05.680
them all the credit for guarding me with one man in game one well in game one i just missed shots

02:59:06.350 --> 02:59:11.170
can they ever try to guard me with one guy again i'll get 20 a half so in the second half they

02:59:11.170 --> 02:59:14.790
dealt me every time i touched the ball and i didn't score and i did a good job of picking

02:59:14.790 --> 02:59:20.430
the defense apart but uh you guys were all riding on coattails after game one i got great shots in

02:59:20.430 --> 02:59:25.300
game one i just didn't make any but ain't no one player can guard me and y'all can write that down

02:59:25.300 --> 02:59:29.900
I missed some shots in game one, but they can't call me with one guy like y'all.

02:59:30.000 --> 02:59:34.480
like to believe so they doubled me every time in the second half and I was able to pick guys out

02:59:34.480 --> 02:59:41.240
and Kevin made some plays but I got him to ball out of the double team. Charles uh Matthew Johnson

02:59:41.240 --> 02:59:46.740
talked about you have to hate your enemy to uh be able to beat him but you guys have transcended

02:59:46.740 --> 02:59:59.740
that to also enjoy this series. Well uh I think that's bold you know yeah you shouldn't hate anybody.

03:00:05.360 --> 03:00:10.570
And listen, we had a chance to win the last game, too.

03:00:10.690 --> 03:00:12.470
We just couldn't make a play down the stretch.

03:00:12.900 --> 03:00:15.750
But tonight, you know, we just didn't let it get like that.

03:00:16.690 --> 03:00:23.270
So everybody was talking, hey, let me tell you, if Michael gets 55, we have a chance to win with a minute to go.

03:00:23.330 --> 03:00:24.850
I'll take that every time on the road.

03:00:26.220 --> 03:00:28.120
But now we're going to the Valley.

03:00:29.130 --> 03:00:29.710
Could be hot.

03:00:30.190 --> 03:00:30.730
It could be real.

03:00:34.970 --> 03:00:36.510
Thank God, want us to win?

03:00:37.320 --> 03:00:38.800
I believe there's such thing as destiny.

03:00:41.790 --> 03:00:45.050
And I told Michael that the other night at dinner, I just believe in my heart.

03:00:45.050 --> 03:00:49.360
I'm not saying that's going to happen, but I believe it 100% that it's just our destiny.

03:00:50.040 --> 03:00:51.060
What was Michael's response?

03:00:53.820 --> 03:00:55.940
He said he read a different Bible than I did.

03:00:57.980 --> 03:00:59.800
Charles, were you a little surprised?

03:01:00.220 --> 03:01:03.240
when they did not come at you offensively,

03:01:03.260 --> 03:01:05.100
when you went to your smaller lineup,

03:01:05.340 --> 03:01:07.120
they had you playing center on defense,

03:01:07.450 --> 03:01:09.240
they had Horace on you also,

03:01:09.280 --> 03:01:11.460
and they did not take shots with Cartwright and Horace?

03:01:12.120 --> 03:01:15.080
Well, I mean, I don't worry too much about what the other team is doing.

03:01:15.080 --> 03:01:16.860
We just try to do what we do best.

03:01:16.940 --> 03:01:21.400
I think what happened is we came out,

03:01:21.560 --> 03:01:24.080
I think the coach wanted me to get off to a good start, and I did.

03:01:24.460 --> 03:01:27.320
And that forces them to double-team me every time.

03:01:27.700 --> 03:01:29.700
And when they're doubling me every time,

03:01:29.700 --> 03:01:29.860
Thank you.

03:01:30.440 --> 03:01:33.140
And if I get the ball to K.J., he's going to make things happen.

03:01:33.220 --> 03:01:35.640
If I get the ball to Ed Marley, he's going to make some things happen.

03:01:36.480 --> 03:01:38.580
Who you been? Helping them take down that plywood?

03:01:39.580 --> 03:01:39.940
Right.

03:01:40.760 --> 03:01:44.540
Charles, can you comment on the play, Richard, how much tonight, the 25 points?

03:01:44.700 --> 03:01:46.460
Richard played really, really well.

03:01:46.740 --> 03:01:53.530
I tell you what, Richard, I think it's a beneficiary of, I think, playing with me and K.J.

03:01:53.650 --> 03:01:57.240
because he's very athletic and he moves well.

03:01:57.440 --> 03:01:58.940
And he wants to score every time.

03:01:58.940 --> 03:01:59.280
so

03:02:00.000 --> 03:02:02.920
So when you play with guys like me who you have to double

03:02:02.920 --> 03:02:05.760
or play with a point guard like Kevin who's penetrating every time,

03:02:05.940 --> 03:02:08.230
it makes the game a lot easier for guys like that.

03:02:09.220 --> 03:02:12.300
What's going to be the key element to beat them in Phoenix,

03:02:12.540 --> 03:02:14.120
something that you haven't done all season?

03:02:15.310 --> 03:02:17.970
Well, I think it's a different mentality now.

03:02:18.830 --> 03:02:22.030
I think we know that we can beat them,

03:02:23.220 --> 03:02:26.300
and we just got to come out and play aggressive.

03:02:27.250 --> 03:02:29.980
I think, you know, other than games,

03:02:30.000 --> 03:02:32.920
Game one, I'm pretty happy with our performances.

03:02:32.940 --> 03:02:37.720
Other than the first quarter of game one, I'm very happy with our performances.

03:02:38.150 --> 03:02:40.470
And I think that, I think it's very important.

03:02:41.210 --> 03:02:44.930
I've said this a hundred times, this team can only go as far as me and Kevin takes it.

03:02:45.430 --> 03:02:49.330
And if we both play well, or one of us play well, we're not going to win.

03:02:49.560 --> 03:02:51.700
But if both of us play well, we're going to beat anybody.

03:02:51.920 --> 03:02:53.920
And that's kind of like Michael and Scotty.

03:02:54.430 --> 03:02:59.910
Charles, do you get the sense that the Bulls are getting worn down by the pace that you guys have set in this game?

03:03:01.440 --> 03:03:04.850
You know, hey, Michael Jordan was tired tonight.

03:03:06.220 --> 03:03:07.260
He was tired tonight.

03:03:08.380 --> 03:03:17.620
And as an offensive player myself, when you get 30, 40, and 55 points, you're tired.

03:03:18.270 --> 03:03:23.610
And everybody was saying the other day, well, we put KJ on him, we put Marlon, and we put Dumas on him.

03:03:24.360 --> 03:03:26.320
Hey, he has to work hard.

03:03:27.110 --> 03:03:28.870
Number one, those guys are very athletic.

03:03:29.050 --> 03:03:29.960
He takes a lot.

03:03:30.120 --> 03:03:38.200
energy to get past those guys and didn't score 55 points on top of that and uh hey he human

03:03:42.910 --> 03:03:44.870
take that shit off the windows

03:03:47.360 --> 03:03:48.760
you don't need it tonight

03:03:58.740 --> 03:03:59.500
you're up

03:04:00.630 --> 03:04:10.920
Come back and take a three-point lead, but did you feel with the way you had defended him up to that point that you were playing a much better game?

03:04:11.180 --> 03:04:16.340
We felt without a doubt we were playing a much better game, and we got up 16, and we really felt we were playing at our tempo.

03:04:16.970 --> 03:04:21.830
And Paxton, it was three for three the first half with three three-pointers, and that's nine big points.

03:04:21.910 --> 03:04:25.430
Had it not been for those shots, we felt good about the way we were playing.

03:04:25.670 --> 03:04:29.920
So even though we lost our lead, we felt that things were okay.

03:04:30.000 --> 03:04:32.360
and certainly in our favor the way the tempo was going.

03:04:32.600 --> 03:04:37.640
Can you explain some of their weaknesses in terms of their bench, in terms of scoring at center?

03:04:37.920 --> 03:04:41.520
Well, I don't know, you know, what we were trying to do as far as exploiting their weaknesses,

03:04:41.520 --> 03:04:46.950
but certainly we felt that all year long our bench has been one of our biggest assets,

03:04:47.070 --> 03:04:51.110
and our depth is something that we hope will really play a factor as this series goes on.

03:04:51.810 --> 03:04:54.980
Kevin, why did you find the middle so weak to drive,

03:04:55.040 --> 03:04:59.620
and it seemed like there was no front line for the Bulls going down the line there.

03:05:00.000 --> 03:05:02.890
I don't know if it was easy. It may have looked easy, but it didn't feel easy.

03:05:03.010 --> 03:05:07.360
I just think when you play a team enough, pretty soon you start finding things that you can do against them.

03:05:07.420 --> 03:05:11.290
And I didn't think the first two games, for me personally or our whole Phoenix team,

03:05:11.410 --> 03:05:12.830
was going to be indicative of the series.

03:05:13.070 --> 03:05:17.170
And that's why you want this series to keep going on because you can pick your spots

03:05:17.170 --> 03:05:21.030
and you see us do different things in this ballgame that we didn't do in the previous games.

03:05:21.330 --> 03:05:23.250
How many of you guys feel you played tonight?

03:05:23.630 --> 03:05:25.190
Will that be a good enough Sunday?

03:05:25.230 --> 03:05:26.910
Do you think they're going to be that much better?

03:05:27.230 --> 03:05:29.070
You're going to have to turn it up even more.

03:05:29.070 --> 03:05:29.910
I think we can.

03:05:30.030 --> 03:05:34.270
it up even more we have to worry about what we need to do we had a goal when we came to chicago

03:05:34.270 --> 03:05:38.370
when people didn't think it could happen and that was to win two games we did that we're going back

03:05:38.370 --> 03:05:46.080
home two games and we haven't won at home yet and we're looking forward to that and we feel that

03:05:46.930 --> 03:05:53.090
these are very good attack you guys have had this whole series i think we really had the floor

03:05:53.090 --> 03:05:58.420
spread very well and we got some big contributions from oliver miller he didn't show up maybe uh

03:05:58.420 --> 03:05:59.840
big and heaviness in it

03:06:00.000 --> 03:06:03.300
in the box scores, but he does a lot of little things out there

03:06:03.300 --> 03:06:05.220
that really make our team that much more effective.

03:06:05.900 --> 03:06:08.970
Charles said that Michael looked tired. Could you sense that?

03:06:09.530 --> 03:06:13.130
I'm not saying anything about Michael to get him upset as he comes to Phoenix.

03:06:13.570 --> 03:06:15.210
All I know is he said he wasn't coming to Phoenix,

03:06:15.250 --> 03:06:17.950
so if he doesn't come to Phoenix, I think the series is over, that's for sure.

03:06:18.670 --> 03:06:22.190
Kevin, you're making the season now. The Suns have won three of four here in Chicago.

03:06:22.190 --> 03:06:25.530
What's been the key to playing here in Chicago?

03:06:26.230 --> 03:06:29.050
I don't know. I just think all year we've been a very good road team,

03:06:29.050 --> 03:06:29.910
man, because we don't.

03:06:30.620 --> 03:06:32.620
We know it's a huge challenge to play on the road.

03:06:32.720 --> 03:06:35.780
I don't think there's anything profound about it.

03:06:35.840 --> 03:06:39.940
We just go out and play hard, and sometimes at home we rely on our home court to win ballgames.

03:06:40.400 --> 03:06:43.040
Can you talk about the importance of rebounding tonight?

03:06:43.300 --> 03:06:47.120
Going into Game 4, Paul Westfeld talked about how important it would be tonight.

03:06:47.280 --> 03:06:50.520
You actually controlled the boards, which allowed you to run.

03:06:50.700 --> 03:06:54.180
Well, we felt there were two things that were really important for us to win this ballgame tonight,

03:06:54.260 --> 03:06:56.140
and they were both on the defensive end of the court.

03:06:56.900 --> 03:06:59.960
One is that we really had to step up and clog the middle and not let...

03:07:00.220 --> 03:07:02.160
Jordan just gets straight past to the basket.

03:07:02.280 --> 03:07:04.530
When he does that, he does it easily.

03:07:04.570 --> 03:07:08.230
He gets people in foul trouble, and it just really puts us at a disadvantage.

03:07:08.470 --> 03:07:11.330
So the big man in our front line really stepped up well today.

03:07:11.510 --> 03:07:14.650
And in the other area that you're talking about, the rebounding with Mark Rust

03:07:14.650 --> 03:07:17.510
and all the other big guys, Dan Marley did an exceptional job

03:07:17.510 --> 03:07:18.850
on the rebounding end of the court.

03:07:18.930 --> 03:07:21.540
It was something that we needed to control if we had a chance.

03:07:28.980 --> 03:07:29.760
Kevin Johnson.

03:07:30.120 --> 03:07:34.690
And tying Richard Dumas for Phoenix scoring honors with 25 points.

03:07:34.850 --> 03:07:37.730
K.J. with 11 of those 25 in the fourth quarter.

03:07:37.970 --> 03:07:42.390
Suns take two of three in Chicago, but the Bulls still lead the series three games to two.

03:07:42.570 --> 03:07:47.320
Suns win game five tonight, final 108 to 98.

03:07:47.320 --> 03:07:52.720
We're waiting for Bulls coach Phil Jackson to approach the podium and talk with the media.

